class.description:
Returned by [method PlayFabMultiplayer.create_match_ticket_async] and [method PlayFabMultiplayer.join_match_ticket_async]. Successful factory results have a non-empty [member ticket_id], so a surfaced successful ticket can be cancelled by id immediately. Ticket progress is pushed through [signal state_changed]. This class contains two distinct numeric spaces. [constant CREATED], [constant STATUS_CHANGED], [constant COMPLETED], [constant CANCELLED], and [constant FAILED] are [b]event kinds[/b] used by [member PlayFabMatchTicketStateChange.kind]. Despite its name, [constant STATUS_CHANGED] is never a ticket status. Compare [member status] and [member PlayFabMatchTicketStateChange.status] against the [code]STATUS_*[/code] constants instead. The native [code]TicketCompleted[/code] record is the sole terminal authority. A terminal [code]TicketStatusChanged[/code] record refreshes the cached [member status] but does not settle create, join, or cancellation operations, emit any event, or destroy the native ticket. Terminal settlement, notification, and destruction wait for [code]TicketCompleted[/code]. A failed completion preserves its native HRESULT in [member PlayFabMatchTicketStateChange.result]. A cancelled status is authoritative: the SDK may complete cancellation with a failure HRESULT, which is reported as a successful [constant CANCELLED] notification. The addon intentionally has no timeout that guesses a missing completion HRESULT; [method PlayFabMultiplayer.shutdown_async] (or a finish-failure reset) remains the escape path if the SDK never delivers completion. The ticket snapshot is refreshed before each accepted change, but the signal stream is not lossless or replayed. Creating-state edges may be suppressed while the ticket id is unavailable, and create/join can return a snapshot that already reached a later status before the caller can connect. Treat the API as level-triggered. Connect the signal, reconcile the current snapshot immediately, and reconcile again on every change regardless of [member PlayFabMatchTicketStateChange.kind]. Handlers must be idempotent. Final status, match id, arrangement string, and properties remain readable after native destruction. [codeblock] ticket.state_changed.connect(_on_ticket_changed) _handle_ticket_status(ticket, ticket.status) # reconcile now
func _on_ticket_changed(change: PlayFabMatchTicketStateChange) -> void: _handle_ticket_status(change.ticket, change.ticket.status)
func _handle_ticket_status(ticket: PlayFabMatchTicket, status: int) -> void: if status == PlayFabMatchTicket.STATUS_WAITING_FOR_PLAYERS: _publish_ticket_id_once(ticket.ticket_id) [/codeblock] [member members] contains only the local users supplied when this client created or joined the ticket. It is not the completed match roster.
